  "methodology": "Conservative same-region engineering estimates for serial provider calls. Google Cloud documents request-rate behavior and latency variables but does not publish per-operation p50, p95, or p99 guarantees; these reviewed values are regression-budget inputs, not provider measurements or an SLA.",
  "limitations": [
    "Actual latency varies with client and bucket location, network path, object size, request rate, access pattern, namespace hotspots, retries, and current service load",
    "Operation totals sum per-request estimates and therefore model the serial critical path; applications that prove bounded parallelism may introduce a separately reviewed model",
    "The byte term assumes approximately 100 MiB/s and is intentionally a planning estimate rather than a Google Cloud performance claim"
  ],
